          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(latkit_s3_requests_total{proto=~\"$proto\",op=\"other\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min(sum(rate(latkit_s3_requests_total{proto=~\"$proto\"}[$__rate_interval])), 0.001)",
          "refId": "A",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "legendFormat": "value"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Requests the operation table did not recognise (РS2). Unlike an HTTP route this is never a cardinality problem — the label set is closed by construction — it is an *ageing* signal: the S3 API grows, and a growing share here means docs/notes-s3proto.md needs a new row (risk 5)."
    },
